<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><b>2025 Equity Incentive Plan</b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><b>&#160;</b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt">The following paragraphs describe
the principal terms of the 2025 Equity Incentive Plan:</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt"><i>Type of Awards.</i> The 2025
Equity Incentive Plan permits the awards of options (including incentive stock options and nonqualified stock options), stock bonus awards,
restricted stock awards, deferred shares, performance awards, and other types of awards approved by the committee.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt"><i>Plan Administration.</i> The
board of directors, or a committee appointed by the board, will administer the 2025 Equity Incentive Plan. The committee may also delegate
the authority to grant and administer awards to one or more officers for eligible persons who are not directors or executive officers.
The plan administrator will determine, among others, the participants to receive awards, the number of shares to be covered by each award,
the form of award agreements, and the terms and conditions of each award.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt"><i>Award Agreement.</i> Awards
granted under the 2025 Equity Incentive Plan are evidenced by a stock option agreement, stock award agreement, or performance agreement,
as applicable, that sets forth the specific terms and conditions of the award. These agreements may specify the term, the vesting schedule,
the provisions applicable in the event that the awardee&#8217;s employment or service terminates, and the administrator&#8217;s authority
to amend, modify, or cancel the award.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt"><i>Eligibility.</i> We may grant
awards to our employees, directors, and consultants. However, incentive stock options may only be granted to our employees or employees
of our parent or subsidiaries.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt"><i>Vesting Schedule.</i> In general,
the plan administrator determines the vesting schedule, which is specified in the relevant award agreement. The vesting may also be further
conditioned upon the attainment of specific performance objectives established by the committee.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt"></p>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 87 -->
    <div style="border-bottom: Black 2pt solid; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->80<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div>
    <div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div>
